      "text": "To find \\( z \\), we need to use the formula for the projection of a vector \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) onto a vector \\(\\mathbf{u}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}}{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{u}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe start by calculating \\(\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 0 + 15 - z = 15 - z\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nUsing these results in the projection formula, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe know this projection is equal to the given vector:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe only component differences between the two vectors are the \\(x\\) components. Clearly:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\cdot (-3) = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( z \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\cdot (-3) = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-3 \\cdot \\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-3 \\cdot (15 - z) = 12\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-45 + 3z = 12\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3z = 57\n\\]\n\n\\[\nz = 19\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( z \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{19}\n\\]",
