      "text": "To find the value of \\( z \\), we need to understand the relationship between any vector and its projection. The projection of a vector \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) onto a vector \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}}{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{u}\n\\]\nHere, the vector \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\). The given projection is:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nFirst, we need to calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 15 - z\n\\]\nNext, we calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\nNow, we can express the projection formula with these dot products:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nWe know this projection equals \\(\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), so we can set up the following equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nSince the vectors on both sides are equal in magnitude and direction (assume the scaler is the same), we can equate the coefficients. Specifically, the coefficient of \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) must be equal:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\nBy simplifying this equation, we get:\n\\[\n15 - z = 12\n\\]\nSolving for \\( z \\):\n\\[\nz = 15 - 12 = 3\n\\]\nThus, the value of \\( z \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
